// Every visible string of the landing page, in the eight languages it is built in.
// Japanese is the source of truth: when a line changes there, the other seven
// have to change with it, or that language goes on describing an older product.
// scripts/build-site.mjs renders one static page per language from this file.
//
// Values are plain text and are escaped when inserted, except for the keys the
// template marks data-i18n-html (headings with <span>/<br>), which are HTML.
//
// Company-profile values are a matter of legal record, so the registered name and
// address are romanised rather than translated, and the kanji form is kept
// wherever it is readable (ja/zh/zh-TW). Each plan is one Stripe Price in JPY
// with a manual USD option: Japanese shows yen, every other language shows the
// US-dollar amount (charged exactly in the US; elsewhere Stripe converts from
// JPY at checkout). JPY stays the canonical price in the structured data.
